    <!-- M7: this config's own bytes now reach the core, when eligible. The old
         wording said Subspace runs "a parsed copy of it, not the file itself",
         which is no longer universally true — this claim is now shown only when
         EditorState.runsAsWritten is true (Task 10 review, Critical 1): an
         ineligible row gets editor_raw_json_read_only_notice below instead, so
         this claim and a rejection string are never on screen together. -->
    <string name="editor_raw_json_notice">
        This server was added from a pasted config file, and Subspace runs that file as written.
        Only the name can be changed — editing the text would risk breaking a config the app
        cannot re-derive.
    </string>

    <!-- Shown instead of editor_raw_json_notice whenever the "runs as written" claim would not
         hold for what actually reaches the core: either this row is not eligible to run as
         written (rejection string shown with it), or the row IS eligible but an app rule set or
         DNS plan is overriding its routing/dns (I2 fix — editor_raw_json_override_warning shown
         with it instead, which contradicts "runs that file as written" if the notice above were
         used). Same read-only/rename explanation in both cases, minus the "runs as written"
         claim. -->
    <string name="editor_raw_json_read_only_notice">
        This server was added from a pasted config file. Only the name can be changed — editing
        the text would risk breaking a config the app cannot re-derive.
    </string>

    <!-- Shown only when this profile runs as written AND an app rule set or a
         custom DNS resolver is active. Task 10 review ruling: names both
         replaced blocks (spec §3 swaps both routing and dns wholesale, not just
         routing rules) and gives a remedy covering both switches, since either
         one alone can trigger this. Deliberately in the user's terms: no tag
         names, no mention of routing/dns blocks as such. -->
    <string name="editor_raw_json_override_warning">
        Your routing and DNS settings replace this file\'s own, so it does not run as written.
        Turn routing off and set DNS back to default to run it exactly as written.
    </string>

